_vars=\"species\", var_name=\"feature\", value_name=\"cm\")\n","sns.boxplot(data=melted, x=\"feature\", y=\"cm\", hue=\"species\", palette=\"viridis\", ax=axes[1])\n","axes[1].set_title(\"Feature ranges by species\")\n","axes[1].tick_params(axis=\"x\", rotation=20)\n","plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"FK3ZM4h-Rnnh","metadata":{"id":"FK3ZM4h-Rnnh"},"source":["**Observations**\n","- *Setosa* is clearly separable from the other two species, mainly through its small petals.\n","- *Versicolor* and *Virginica* overlap a little, so these two are where classification errors are most likely.\n","- Petal length and petal width are the most informative features and are strongly correlated with each other."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"QDettjT_Rnnh","metadata":{"id":"QDettjT_Rnnh"},"source":["## 3. Feature scaling and train / test split\n","- **Shuffle before splitting** to remove order bias. The raw Iris file is sorted by species.\n","- **Stratify** so each class keeps the same proportion in both sets.\n","- **StandardScaler** (mean = 0, variance = 1) is placed inside a `Pipeline`, so it is fitted on the training data only. This prevents data leakage from the test set."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"Z5xFzQ9SRnni","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":9,"status":"ok","timestamp":1790739115770,"user":{"displayName":"I.Rihana Sulthana","userId":"13617876133183882723"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"Z5xFzQ9SRnni","outputId":"a4b87d75-19d6-49a8-8efa-6de96f33fe09"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Training set: 120 samples (80%)\n","Test set    : 30 samples (20%)\n","\n","Test class counts:\n"," species\n","setosa        10\n","virginica     10\n","versicolor    10\n"]}],"source":["X = df.drop(columns=\"species\")\n","y = df[\"species\"]\n","\n","X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n","    X, y, test_size=0.20, shuffle=True, stratify=y, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n","\n","print(f\"Training set: {len(X_train)} samples (80%)\")\n","print(f\"Test set    : {len(X_test)} samples (20%)\")\n","print(\"\\nTest class counts:\\n\", y_test.value_counts().to_string())"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"xsPYos6gRnni","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":155},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":400,"status":"ok","timestamp":1790739116172,"user":{"displayName":"I.Rihana Sulthana","userId":"13617876133183882723"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"xsPYos6gRnni","outputId":"01c621d3-7468-4b04-e202-3e15cdbf7be7"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1320x418 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# Visual proof of what scaling does\n","scaled = pd.DataFrame(StandardScaler().fit_transform(X_train), columns=X.columns)\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 3.8), sharey=False)\n","sns.boxplot(data=X_train, palette=\"viridis\", ax=axes[0]); axes[0].set_title(\"Before scaling\")\n","sns.boxplot(data=scaled,  palette=\"viridis\", ax=axes[1]); axes[1].set_title(\"After StandardScaler\")\n","for a in axes: a.tick_params(axis=\"x\", rotation=20)\n","plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"vKMBwI-1Rnnj","metadata":{"id":"vKMBwI-1Rnnj"},"source":["## 4. Tune the engine: choosing K\n","K-Nearest Neighbors classifies a flower by a majority vote among its K closest training samples. A very small K overfits to noise, and a very large K underfits. K is chosen using **5-fold cross-validation on the training set only**."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"i952PLHvRnnk","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":282},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":0,"status":"ok","timestamp":1790739118730,"user":{"displayName":"I.Rihana Sulthana","userId":"13617876133183882723"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"i952PLHvRnnk","outputId":"8e0b8a0b-c562-442b-af67-5c1871f5c3f1"},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 880x495 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"metadata":{"tags":null},"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Optimal K = 3 (CV accuracy 0.967)\n"]}],"source":["cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n","k_values = list(range(1, 31))\n","errors = []\n","for k in k_values:\n","    pipe = Pipeline([(\"scaler\", StandardScaler()), (\"knn\", KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=k))])\n","    errors.append(1 - cross_val_score(pipe, X_train, y_train, cv=cv, scoring=\"accuracy\").mean())\n","\n","best_k = k_values[int(np.argmin(errors))]\n","\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4.5))\n","ax.plot(k_values, errors, marker=\"o\", ms=4)\n","ax.scatter([best_k], [min(errors)], s=180, facecolors=\"none\", edgecolors=\"tab:red\", linewidths=2, label=f\"Optimal K = {best_k}\")\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"K (number of neighbors)\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"Cross-validation error rate\")\n","ax.set_title(\"Choosing K: the elbow\"); ax.legend()\n","plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n","print(f\"Optimal K = {best_k} (CV accuracy {1 - min(errors):.3f})\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"7KFRjUiWRnnk","metadata":{"id":"7KFRjUiWRnnk"},"source":["## 5. Build the model: Instantiate → Fit → Predict"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"g-o50n49Rnnl","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":0,"status":"ok","timestamp":1790739118643,"user":{"displayName":"I.Rihana Sulthana","userId":"13617876133183882723"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"g-o50n49Rnnl","outputId":"2d37d9c0-b3a0-4451-c341-7fce76f53443"},"outputs":[{"metadata":{"tags":null},"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Model trained.\n","Sample predictions: ['setosa', 'virginica', 'versicolor', 'versicolor', 'setosa', 'versicolor', 'setosa', 'setosa']\n","Actual labels     : ['setosa', 'virginica', 'versicolor', 'versicolor', 'setosa', 'versicolor', 'setosa', 'setosa']\n"]}],"source":["model = Pipeline([\n","    (\"scaler\", StandardScaler()),\n","    (\"knn\", KNeighborsClassifier(n_neighbors=best_k)),      # INSTANTIATE: build the frame\n","])\n","model.fit(X_train, y_train)                                 # FIT: memorize the map\n","predictions = model.predict(X_test)                         # PREDICT: apply logic\n","\n","print(\"Model trained.\")\n","print(\"Sample predictions:\", [str(p) for p in predictions[:8]])\n","print(\"Actual labels     :\", [str(v) for v in y_test.iloc[:8]])"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"B7IN-ODVRnnm","metadata":{"id":"B7IN-ODVRnnm"},"source":["## 6. Output validation\n","Accuracy alone can be misleading, especially on imbalanced data. The confusion matrix, precision, recall and F1 give the full picture."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"9NXIZYGgRnnn","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":206},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":0,"status":"ok","timestamp":1790739118817,"user":{"displayName":"I.Rihana Sulthana","userId":"13617876133183882723"},"user_tz":-330},"id":"9NXIZYGgRnnn","outputId":"eae18991-7fc7-45bd-ffbb-9a8217da2a31"},"outputs":[{"data":{"application/vnd.google.colaboratory.intrinsic+json":{"summary":"{\n  \"name\": \"              \\\"Score\\\": [acc, prec, rec, f1]})\",\n  \"rows\": 4,\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Metric\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"string\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 4,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"Precision (macro)\",\n          \"F1 score (macro)\",\n          \"Accuracy\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"column\": \"Score\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"number\",\n        \"std\": 0.0054999999999999485,\n        \"min\": 0.933,\n        \"max\": 0.944,\n        \"num_unique_values\": 2,\n        \"samples\": [\n          0.944,\n          0.933\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\